    </p>

    <h3>2. Types of SMS Communications</h3>
    <p>
      If you have consented to receive text messages from PrimeCare Network, LLC, you may receive
      messages related to the following:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Conversations (external):</strong> External client and patient communications (such
        as appointment reminders, scheduling updates, follow-up inquiries, and billing
        notifications)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Conversations (between employees):</strong> Internal communications between
        employees.
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p><strong>Example Message:</strong></p>
    <p>
      “Hello, this is a friendly reminder of your upcoming appointment with PrimeCare Network, LLC
      on [Date] at [Time]. You can reply STOP to opt out of SMS messaging from PrimeCare Network,
      LLC at any time.”
    </p>

    <h3>3. Message Frequency</h3>
    <p>
      Message frequency may vary depending on the type of communication. For example, you may
